@call c05 stroke start=16:48:20
@patient age=71 sex=male weight_kg=88 complaint="sudden right sided weakness and trouble speaking" allergies=NKDA home_meds="aspirin, amlodipine" history="hypertension"
@traps stroke; CVA
RD: Medic 9, possible stroke, seventy-one year old male.  >> dispatch:possible stroke "possible stroke"
GAP 3
M1: Medic 9 on scene.  >> time:eTimes.06 "on scene"
GAP 3
BY: He was fine at lunch, then at four fifteen he dropped his coffee and his face went funny.
M1: Last known well sixteen fifteen.  >> status:last known well 16:15 "Last known well sixteen fifteen"
M1: Sir, smile for me. Squeeze my hands. Right side facial droop, right arm drift, slurred speech.  >> status:facial droop "Right side facial droop"; status:arm drift "right arm drift"; status:slurred speech "slurred speech"
TAP knock +label
M2: BP 188 over 102, heart rate 84, sat 97.  >> vital:bp=188/102 "BP 188 over 102"; vital:hr=84 "heart rate 84"; vital:spo2=97 "sat 97"
GAP 2
TAP snap +label
M2: Sugar's 136.  >> vital:bgl=136 "Sugar's 136"
M1: BE-FAST positive. Calling a stroke alert, let's load and go.  >> proc:stroke scale "BE-FAST positive"
GAP 4
M1: Transporting to Regional.  >> time:eTimes.09 "Transporting"
GAP 10
TAP button -
GAP 12
M2: Eighteen in the left AC.  >> proc:IV access "Eighteen in the left AC"
GAP 5
TAP button +label
M2: GCS is 14, he's confused on verbal.  >> vital:gcs=14 "GCS is 14"
GAP 6
M1: Don't give him anything by mouth. Keep the head of the bed up thirty.
GAP 8
M2: Repeat pressure 182 over 98.  >> vital:bp=182/98 "182 over 98"
GAP 8
TAP knock +label
M1: Arrived at Regional, straight to CT.  >> time:eTimes.11 "Arrived at Regional"
GAP 4
M1: Handing off to the stroke team.  >> time:eTimes.12 "Handing off"
